Following the acoplanar $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay, the $D_s^{-}$ particle produces a $D_s^{*-}$ particle in a short sequence. By using the shape of the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ form factor, we can determine the parity of the $D_s^{*0}$ particle. The $dE/dx$ profile of the $D_s^{-}$ particle helps distinguish it from other similar particles. With a sample of 0.334 billion $B ar{B}$ pairs, the experiment recorded 14 $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decays and 5 acoplanar $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decays. The form factor ratio $Rpc = \xi_{B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*0}}(0)/\xi_{B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{0}}(0))$ was measured to be $0.85 \pm 0.16 (\stat) \pm 0.02 (\sys)$. The $D_s^{*0}$ particle's parity was confirmed to be positive, matching previous findings.
